Explanation of the patch:

1. We locate the initial `.filter(evt => { … })` on `tabTrace.processEvents`.
2. Right after we reject anything that isn’t `blink.user_timing`, we insert a new guard:
   ```js
   if (evt.name.startsWith('ad_') || evt.name.startsWith('goog_')) {
     return false;
   }
   ```
3. Any event whose name begins with `ad_` or `goog_` is immediately dropped, so the rest of the user-timing audit only sees your own marks/measures.
